  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch our situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950896/assets/e13444351bb092ced6fc788ae921622f154a267e9544e928700736a53a259fc6.png)\n\nThe area $A$ under the graph can be approximated using the right Riemann sum with step size $\u0394x=0.5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA\u2248(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{\u23de}{f(0.5)+f(1)+f(1.5)+f(2)}})\\cdot {{\u0394x}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{width}}\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $f(x)$ at each point:\n\n| $x$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $3.75$ | $3$ | $1.75$ | $0$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain the following approximation for our area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u2248(3.75+3+1.75+0)\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =8.5\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =4.25\\end{aligned}\n$$",
